course: dictionary
lesson: 4787
title: Many meanings of one word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word human has more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one. Read the words around it. «Rights are things every person should have just for being human.» Here human means a person: a man, woman or child.
explain: Human can also describe things to do with people. Look at «The human body is made of many organs.» Human is a describing word here, telling you which body we mean. Ask yourself: is the word a thing, or is it describing one? That answers the question.
explain: Sometimes human means having normal feelings and weaknesses. «It is only human to make mistakes.» Everyone gets things wrong sometimes, so the sentence means that making mistakes is normal. Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: A human is a person: a man, woman or child.
fact: Human can also describe things to do with people, such as the human body or human rights.
fact: Scientists call humans mammals, and their scientific name is Homo sapiens.
fact: «Rights are things every person should have just for being human.» Children have special rights under a United Nations agreement.
fact: Human can mean having normal feelings and weaknesses, as in «only human».
exercise: «Humans have tried all of these ways to run whole countries.» What does humans mean here? | Countries | Animals that can run fast | Robots | *People
exercise: «It is only human to make mistakes.» What does this sentence mean? | It means you are a robot | Only animals make mistakes | *It is normal to make mistakes, because everyone does | Mistakes are not allowed
exercise: In «The human body is made of many organs», which word describes the body? | organs | *human | many | body
test: What is a human in «Every person should have rights just for being human»? | *A person | A machine | A type of food | A tree
test: What is the scientific name for humans? | Mammal sapiens | Sapiens humanus | *Homo sapiens | Homo robot
exam: Which phrase is about the rights every person should have? | human race | *human rights | only human | human body
